     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Conduct and facilitate community-based adaptation interventions in 13 coastal states. 

2. Project implementation structures to be established: Project Steering Committees and Project Management Units at 
 National, State, and District level.

3. Conducting an in-depth baseline assessment for 3 project states

4. Initiating the in-depth study on Gender-sensitive vulnerability assessment for the 13 coastal states 

5. Conducting a mid-term review of the project (as per GCF legal deadline)

6. Organise 1 national dialogue to share experiences in EBA and community adaptation to climate change in the 
 coastal zone.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.    Project implementation structures like Project Steering Committees and Project Management Units established at the National, State, and District levels

2.   Successfully achieved restoration of 1025 Ha of mangroves and 500 Ha of coastal watersheds and impacted around 21,000 beneficiaries through livelihood activities in the project landscapes.

3.   Initiated an in-depth baseline assessment for the 3 project states.

4.   Initiated an in-depth study on Gender-sensitive vulnerability assessment for the 13 coastal states.

5.   Conducted a mid-term review of the project (as per GCF legal deadline)

6.   One National Workshop on &#x201c;Sustainable Coastal Management&#x201d; was organised at Bhubaneswar. Over 200 participants from 13 coastal States/ UTs, Central Ministries, Experts from academia, research institutions, NGOs and students working in the sector deliberated on various aspects of sustainable coastal management.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Conduct and facilitate community-based adaptation interventions in 13 coastal states. 
2. Project implementation structures to be established: Project Steering Committees and Project Management Units at national, state, district and landscape level.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Studies and assessments have been initiated at national and state level to facilitate ecosystem and community based interventions in the 13 coastal states, with a particular focus on the three target states- Andhra Pradesh, Odisha and Maharashtra. These include &#x2013; (a) study on completed and on-going Government schemes and network opportunities; (b) vulnerability assessments of the Indian coastal states at district level, and (c) Development of a communication strategy and action plan.
2. Project implementation structures established. This includes the setting up of the state project management units in Odisha and Maharashtra (state and district level). The mechanism for project steering committees was shared with all partners. The first national project steering committee took place on Aug 5, 2020, with participation of key relevant stakeholders.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The project will initiate the Vulnerability Assessment of all coastal states. 
2. The three states will be enagaging local NGOs to carry out ecosystem restoration and sustainable livelihood activities on field. These activities will further be built upon in the following years to acheive the overall project outputs.
3. States will also be initiating participatory planning in target landscapes (by engaging local NGOs) to produce Target Landscape Integrated Management Plans 
4. The project will also see the initiation of establishment of co-management structures (through local NGOs, CBOs, SHGs, etc.) in target landscapes to foster community support for and participation in conservation and restoration activities. 5. Technical Support to selected beneficiary groups on identified climate-adaptive livelihoods and value chains will also be provided through the project.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to changes in the funding mechanism of the project (as requested by MoEFCC), the fund transfer to Odisha and Maharashtra took place in October / November 2021. States are now initiating implementation of activities as per the AWP 2021-22.. These include the delineation of project landscapes as well as engaging with NGOs for ecosystem restoration and sustainable livelihoods as well.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
